The Funnel workflow helps move from “this stage looks weak” to a test that has a reason to exist. A marketer selects a stage or segment, reviews the measurements and asks for possible explanations. AI suggestions use that selected finding, its dates and its evidence to propose hypotheses and tests.

The marketer reviews a suggestion before applying it to the editable draft. Applying it does not save the hypothesis or start an experiment. Existing draft text requires an explicit replacement choice; saving and planning the test remain separate decisions. This keeps the observation, the possible cause and the proposed test distinct.
